::node[meeting_copilot]
->[:role=skill]
->[:keywords=meeting, prep, debrief, notes, agenda, calendar, minutes, google calendar]

::dense
Copilot for Calendar events: pre-meeting context briefs and post-meeting structured minutes.

::steps
1. Ask the user if they need "Prep" or "Debrief" for an upcoming/recent meeting.
2. If "Prep":
   a. Fetch the specific calendar event.
   b. Extract attendee email addresses.
   c. Use Gmail search to find the 3 most recent email threads involving those attendees.
   d. Summarize the context and display it to the user.
3. If "Debrief":
   a. Ask the user to provide raw, unstructured meeting notes.
   b. Structure the notes into Professional Meeting Minutes (Decisions, Action Items, Next Steps).
   c. Create a new Google Doc via the Drive SDK with the structured minutes.
   d. Draft a Gmail message to all meeting attendees containing the summary and the Google Doc link, saving it to Drafts for user review.
